1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vistahm '''Wikipedia'''] page of her brother, Vistahm:
2 CONT
2 CONT "A sister of Vistahm had even married the Sasanian shah Hormizd IV (r. 579–590), and was the mother of Hormizd's heir, Khosrau II.[1][2]"
2 CONT
2 CONT =References=
2 CONT
2 CONT # Pourshariati (2008), pp. 106–108
2 CONT # Shapur Shahbazi (1989), BESṬĀM O BENDŌY
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Pourshariati, Parvaneh (2008). Decline and Fall of the Sasanian Empire: The Sasanian-Parthian Confederacy and the Arab Conquest of Iran. London and New York: I.B. Tauris. ISBN 978-1-84511-645-3.
2 CONT * Shapur Shahbazi, A. (1989). "BESṬĀM O BENDŌY". Encyclopaedia Iranica, Vol. IV, Fasc. 2. pp. 180–182. Retrieved 13 August 2013.
